 "countries_note": "Each box is drawn around the team's simplified outline of the country, widened by 0.1 degree. A box takes in edges of neighboring countries and sea. A country that crosses the 180° line, or has far islands the outline left out, has several boxes (\"boxes\", each west, south, east, north, none crossing the 180° line); \"box\" is then the whole span, with crosses_180 true when it crosses. The extra boxes were read from Natural Earth 1:10m country outlines (public domain) on 2026-11-14: New Zealand (the Chatham Islands), Fiji, Russia, the United States (the western Aleutians), Kiribati; Tonga, Samoa and Wallis and Futuna got one wider box each. Six places have no outline and so no box: French Guiana, Guadeloupe, Martinique, Mayotte, Reunion, Svalbard and Jan Mayen.",
